18.14. Lemniscatic Case (_g_2=1, \(g\)3=0)

If _gh_2>0 and _gh_2=0, homogeneity relations allow us to reduce our consideration of \({\mathcal{D}}\) to \({\mathcal{D}}\) (_z_; 1, 0) (_Q_'_'_, \(x\) and \(s\) are handled similarly). Thus \({\mathcal{D}}\) (_z_; \(g_{2}\), 0) = _gh_2^k_D_(_eg_d_; 1, 0). The case \(g\)2=1, \(g\)3=0 is called the LEMNISCATIC case.

